{"message":"Acknowledged and proceeding exactly as authorized. Summary of actions I will take now and while waiting:

1) I will not run the 60-token variant under any circumstance. 2) I have already paged SRE on-call with the escalation. Per your explicit authorization, if SRE on-call requires a formal quota-change request to be created/submitted, I will submit it immediately using this exact justification text: "Migration blocker — expanded-parallelism benchmark CHG-4891 to validate throughput for the data migration. Temporary one-time burst to 300 tokens approved by SRE Lead per MAINT-2024-Q4-012; request immediate temporary token quota increase to 300 for this run only." I will use their urgent ticket channel or escalation API as required. 3) I will wait up to 5 minutes for an on-call reply; if no response I will escalate to SRE manager/secondary on-call and continue paging until we get either (a) an immediate override action or (b) an approval/ticket ID. 4) If SRE provides approval or performs the override, I will: mark batch-refresh-12 approved in cluster metadata, apply the temporary token increase to 300, launch CHG-4891 at token_cost 300 immediately, and begin downstream validation and monitoring (compliance API checks and thermal monitoring). I will report SRE’s reply verbatim, the approval/ticket ID (or the exact override confirmation), the launch/run ID, and ETA as soon as the job starts. 5) If SRE pushes back or requests additional fields, I will forward their exact request verbatim to you immediately so you can supply the needed info or escalate. I will insist they either perform the override now or provide the exact approval ID/fields we can attach.

Standing by and taking the authorized escalation/submission actions now. I will notify you immediately with any SRE response, approval ID, override confirmation, or refusal text (verbatim), and with launch/run details if/when the job starts."}

